The FujiNet NES cartridge boots .nes images: CONFIG mounts one and the
ESP32 (here, the RS232 PC runtime) must push it to the cartridge over the DBC
stream like any other cartridge ROM. discover_mediatype() only knows ROM,
BIN, INT and ITV (and CHF upstream), so a .nes file mounted as a plain disk
image and the cartridge waited forever for BOOT_READY. Add NES. Upstream
as fujinet-firmware da3973c10 on nes-bringup; carried here until the pin
(cmake/Dependencies.cmake) moves to a commit that has it.

--- a/lib/media/rs232/diskType.cpp
+++ b/lib/media/rs232/diskType.cpp
@@ -77,8 +77,12 @@
         // replaces the previous disksize==8192||16384||32768 heuristic
         // (rs232Disk::mount()), which misfired on any file of those exact
         // sizes regardless of extension and missed every other ROM size.
+        // NES is the iNES cartridge image the FujiNet NES cartridge maps
+        // with its own nesmap; it carries its own header, so extension
+        // alone is unambiguous here too.
         if (strcasecmp(ext, "ROM") == 0 || strcasecmp(ext, "BIN") == 0 ||
-            strcasecmp(ext, "INT") == 0 || strcasecmp(ext, "ITV") == 0)
+            strcasecmp(ext, "INT") == 0 || strcasecmp(ext, "ITV") == 0 ||
+            strcasecmp(ext, "NES") == 0)
         {
             return MEDIATYPE_ROM;
         }
